Third-party components
----------------------

This repository does not bundle any third-party software or model files.
The following components are installed separately as dependencies
(see pyproject.toml) and are used by the M17 Japanese register rules:

- GiNZA (ginza 5.2.0, ja-ginza 5.2.0) - MIT License
  https://github.com/megagonlabs/ginza
  The ja-ginza model lists the following training resources in its
  meta.json. Users of the model should check these terms themselves:
  - UD_Japanese-BCCWJ r2.8 - CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
    https://github.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_Japanese-BCCWJ
  - GSK2014-A (2019) - individually defined commercial license
    https://www.gsk.or.jp/catalog/gsk2014-a/
  - SudachiDict_core, chiVe - Apache License 2.0
- SudachiPy 0.6.11, SudachiDict-core - Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/WorksApplications/SudachiPy
- spaCy 3.7.5 - MIT License

configs/japanese_register_rules.yaml is an original rule set written with
reference to "Keigo no Shishin" (Council for Cultural Affairs, 2007); it
contains no text reproduced from that document.
